      "title": "Pigments & Light Absorption",
      "competency": "STEM_BIO11/12-IIa-j-2, -3",
      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Describe the major features of photosynthesis.</li><li>Identify the pigments involved.</li><li>Explain light absorption and reflection.</li><li>Relate pigments to their roles.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Chlorophyll a</strong> — primary pigment; absorbs blue-violet and red.</li><li><strong>Chlorophyll b</strong> — accessory pigment; absorbs blue and orange.</li><li><strong>Carotenoids</strong> — accessory pigments; absorb blue-green; protect chlorophyll.</li><li><strong>Action spectrum</strong> — wavelengths that drive photosynthesis.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. Photosynthesis Overview</h4><p>6CO₂ + 6H₂O + light → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂</p><p>Occurs in chloroplasts. Two stages: light reactions (thylakoid) and Calvin cycle (stroma).</p><h4>B. Pigments</h4><table><thead><tr><th>Pigment</th><th>Absorbs</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Chlorophyll a</td><td>Blue-violet, red</td><td>Primary pigment</td></tr><tr><td>Chlorophyll b</td><td>Blue, orange</td><td>Accessory pigment</td></tr><tr><td>Carotenoids</td><td>Blue-green</td><td>Accessory + photoprotection</td></tr></tbody></table><h4>C. Why Leaves Are Green</h4><p>Chlorophyll reflects green light — that's why we see leaves as green.</p>",
